By default, tk add creates an accepted task Ticket with unset Priority.
.B \-\-triage
captures work that needs evaluation before it is suitable to take on, with or
without Priority. Ranked triage work remains excluded from
.B tk next
and cannot be started or promoted until accepted.
.PP
Supply a message with
.B \-m
or
.BR \-F ;
bare
.B tk add
does not open an editor.
.PP
The first paragraph becomes the title. Later paragraphs become the body. An
empty message aborts creation.
.PP
On successful Ticket creation,
.B tk add
prints:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Created Ticket: <display-id> - <title>
Kind: task|bug
Priority: P0|P1|P2|P3|unset
Effort: low|medium|high
Status: open
Parent: <container-display-id>
.fi
.RE
.PP
A triage Ticket also prints
.BR "Selection: triage" .
The
.B Effort:
line is printed only when
.B \-\-effort
is supplied. The
.B Parent:
line is printed only when
.B \-\-parent
is supplied, and it uses the Container's current Display ID even when the
argument was an Alias.
.PP
On successful Epic creation,
.B tk add
prints:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Created Epic: <display-id> - <title>
Status: open
.fi
.RE
